## C.11 — Test the fallback

```bash
# 1. Check health
curl -s localhost:3000/api/gateway/health | jq
# Expect: mode=sandbox, providers all configured=false (no env yet)

# 2. In sandbox, send works:
curl -sX POST localhost:3000/api/mobile-money/send \
  -H "x-api-key: BIZ_KEY" -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"phone":"0961234567","amount":100}' | jq '.transaction.status'
# "successful"

# 3. In live mode with only primary broken, verify fallback kicks in:
MOMO_MODE=live MOMO_PROVIDER=flutterwave MOMO_FALLBACK=mtn \
FLW_SECRET_KEY=INVALID node api/index.js
# (in another terminal)
curl -sX POST localhost:3000/api/mobile-money/send \
  -H "x-api-key: BIZ_KEY" -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"phone":"0961234567","amount":100}' | jq '.transaction.raw._fallbackFrom'
# "flutterwave" → confirms fallback attempted
# If MTN also unconfigured: error "both providers failed"
```

